{ isc_pattern_matcher - the ISC's pattern matcher (a DSEE derived object
  of the iscg_input description; cc.a88k only): pattern_matcher tries
  every rule whose pattern a solution matches (its kind, for a chain
  rule; a proper_subtree's IL operator and its children's kinds,
  nested patterns included) and hard_work applies each: the rule's
  pass-1 action makes the new solution, which is compared with the
  solutions of the parent (the similar or dominated one dropped) and
  queued on the work list (pass_1's cross_product_to_solutions_of_
  parent repeats pattern_matcher on it: the chain rules).

  Generated by tools/iscg_gen.py from the rule file
  (moon_unit/isc_prism_dervobjs/dseeaggs/iscg_input/rules/*.isc): do not
  edit; change the rule file or the generator's fixed text
  (tools/iscg_text.py) and regenerate.  tools/iscg_gen.py --check (in
  the gate) fails when this file and the rule file disagree.

  Image addresses (DOMAIN C 6.9; cc.a88k only):
    cc.m68k   cc.a88k
    --------  0x20042C  hard_work
    --------  0x200D6E  pattern_matcher
  A5 0x4800BC: the module's data, the pass-1 action table (+0x000, by
  rule), the flags by rule (+0x8D0 check_permissible, +0xB08
  no_could_deadlock_child) and the byte at +0xB04
  (pm_proper_subtree_seen); +0x8CC four bytes nothing reads.  (-4,A5)
  is the run time's output.  The counters and trace switches are
  isc_user_routines' (isc_var_externs.ins.pas: +0x2F8, +0x354, +0x356).

  Rev 8.89's shape that dpc does not reproduce (best effort): the last
  try of an arm shares one call of hard_work (`pea rule; bra') and arms
  with the same tail jump into one another (cross-jumping), and a
  constant compared twice in a try is loaded once (`moveq #8,D0').

  The writes are dpc gap 4 (docs/dpc-gaps.md 4).

  Not known from the original: the parameters', locals' and module
  data's names (from the traces where they print them), the action
  routines' names (docs/questions.md 266). }
